(g)
"micro-insurance policy" means an insurance policy sold under a plan which has been specifically approved by the
Authority as a micro-insurance product;
(h)
"micro-insurance product" includes a general micro-insurance product or life insurance product, proposal form and all
marketing materials in respect thereof;
(i)
all words and expressions used herein and not defined but defined in the Insurance Act, 1938 (
4 of 1938
), or in the Insurance Regulatory and Development Authority Act, 1999 (
41 of 1999
) or in any Rules or Regulations made there-under shall have the meanings respectively assigned to them in those Acts
or Rules or Regulations.
